    "excerpt": "The Teachers Registration Council of Nigeria (TRCN) administers the Professional Qualifying Examination (PQE) for all teachers in Nigeria. This exam is now comp…",
    "body": [
      "The Teachers Registration Council of Nigeria (TRCN) administers the Professional Qualifying Examination (PQE) for all teachers in Nigeria. This exam is now compulsory. Every teacher in a public or private school must pass it and register with the TRCN to practice legally. The PQE is computer-based. It is offered at approved CBT centres across the country. The exam is divided into categories based on your qualification and teaching level. Category A is for holders of a PhD in Education or a related field. Category B is for master’s degree holders. Category C is for bachelor’s degree holders. Category D is for NCE holders. The questions cover professional knowledge, subject-specific pedagogy, and the TRCN code of conduct. Registration is done through the TRCN online portal. You upload your certificates, a passport photograph, and your teaching service letter. The fee varies by category. The exam holds in batches throughout the year. You must register early to secure your preferred date and centre. To prepare, download the TRCN PQE syllabus from the council’s website. Study the Teachers’ Handbook and the National Teacher Education Policy. Revise the subject you teach. The pedagogy section asks how to teach, not just what to teach. Use past questions available from registered study centres or online forums. The exam is not extremely difficult, but it requires preparation. Do not underestimate it.",
      "Passing the PQE leads to full registration and a license to teach. This license must be renewed periodically. The TRCN conducts spot checks in schools. Unregistered teachers face sanctions. Get certified."
    ],
    "source": "Teachers Registration Council of Nigeria – www.trcn.gov.ng",
