      "The Federal Ministry of Education, through the National Universities Commission (NUC) and JAMB, has issued a new policy directive for the 2026/2027 academic session Post-UTME screening. Institutions are now required to complete their Post-UTME exercises within a unified window and to publish cut-off marks transparently.",
      "In a circular dated 30 June 2026, the ministry directed all universities, polytechnics, and colleges of education to conduct the screening of candidates between 1 October and 14 November 2026. No institution is permitted to hold Post-UTME outside this period without special approval. The circular also mandates that each institution publish its departmental cut-off marks on its website and the JAMB Central Admissions Processing System (CAPS) before the screening begins. The policy change aims to eliminate the practice of hidden or arbitrary cut-off marks that disadvantage candidates. Institutions must now use a clear formula combining UTME score, Post-UTME score, and O-Level grades to compute the aggregate. The aggregate and admission list must be uploaded to CAPS within 72 hours of the screening.",
