    "excerpt": "WAEC WASSCE rewards students who understand patterns. Certain topics appear almost every year. Knowing them gives you an edge. This guide covers the core strate…",
    "body": [
      "WAEC WASSCE rewards students who understand patterns. Certain topics appear almost every year. Knowing them gives you an edge. This guide covers the core strategies.",
      "Know the Format. WASSCE has objective (Paper 1), essay/theory (Paper 2), and practical (Paper 3 for sciences). Each paper tests different skills. Objective requires speed and accuracy. Essay requires clear explanations and step-by-step workings. Practical requires hands-on familiarity. Repeated Topics (Core Subjects).",
      "● English: Essay writing (argumentative, narrative, formal letter), comprehension, summary, lexis and structure (concord, idioms).",
      "● Mathematics: Sets, quadratic equations, circle theorems, trigonometry, statistics, mensuration. Graph questions appear every year.",
      "● Biology: Cell structure, nutrition, respiration, reproduction, ecology, genetics. Diagrams of the heart, eye, ear, and flower are constant.",
      "● Chemistry: Atomic structure, periodic table, bonding, electrolysis, organic chemistry, rates of reaction. Practicals test titration and salt analysis.",
      "● Physics: Motion, waves, electricity, electromagnetism. Calculations and graph interpretation are key.",
      "● Economics: Demand and supply, cost and revenue, national income, money and banking, inflation, international trade. Diagrams are your friend.",
      "● Government: Types of government, constitutions, organs of government, Nigerian political history, electoral systems.",
      "Study Approach. Use the WAEC syllabus as a checklist. For each topic, read your textbook, then solve at least five past questions. Do this topic by topic. After covering all topics, take full timed papers.",
      "Essay Writing Tips. In exams, spend 5 minutes planning your essay. Write a clear introduction, well-developed body paragraphs, and a conclusion. Use simple, correct English. Do not use slang. Neat handwriting matters for paper-based marking.",
      "Practical Preparation. If you are a science student, attend all practical classes. Watch videos of experiments online if your school lacks equipment. Know the procedure, observations, and inferences for common experiments. For technical drawing, practice with the correct instruments.",
      "One Month Before. Solve past questions from 2015 to 2025. Mark yourself honestly. Focus on topics where you consistently lose marks. Use the Highscore platform to test your objective speed. In the final week, do a complete mock run of all papers.",
      "WASSCE is predictable to those who prepare. Master the patterns. Put in the work. Your results will reflect your effort."
    ],
